{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And your valuation shall be according to its seed.</b> Not according to its value — one a good field and one a poor field, the redemption of their consecration is the same — a kor of barley for fifty shekels — so the verse decrees; and that is when he comes to redeem it at the beginning of the jubilee. And if he comes to redeem it in the middle, he gives according to the reckoning — a sela and a pundyon per year — because it is consecrated only for the count of jubilee years: if it is redeemed, well and good; and if not, the treasurer sells it for these monies to another, and it stands in the hand of the buyer until the jubilee like all other sold fields, and when it goes out of his hand it returns to the priests of that watch in which the jubilee falls, and is divided among them. This is the law stated regarding one who consecrates a field, and now I shall set it out in the order of the verses:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:57.245917333Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}